description:
Split from CQ-C07 (task-93dee42f71db4a6a8e47a8de052ad411) on 2026-10-27 by architect-2c9d5121, beside CQ-C07a (task-a50bf5b5d9a4442b88a33554ee5b967f). It consumes C07a's contract: PlanSourceBasis, PlanningEntry, PlanReuseRecord and PlanReuseDecision in types/schema.ts, and readPlanSourceBasis, readPlanningEntry and readPlanReuseRecord in context/planReuseState.ts. CQ-C07 then wires this library into claim, wait and get_context.

Objective: decide whether an approved plan can be reused unchanged, reused with a context refresh, or sent back to an architect. The decision uses daemon state plus committed Git bytes and comes with stable reason codes. This row is a library only: it writes no state and schedules nothing.

Deliverable: a new file, packages/moe-daemon/src/context/planReuse.ts, exporting the four functions below.

1. planReuseView(task). Pure; reads daemon state only, through C07a's decoders. Returns { decision: PlanReuseDecision | 'pending'; reasons: string[] } | null.
   - It returns null when the task has no implementationPlan steps. It also returns null when the status is not PLANNING and no record matches the current planRevision.
   - A decoded planReuse record whose planRevision equals the task's planRevision (in PLANNING, also requiring record.entrySeq === planningEntry.seq) answers with its own decision and reasons.
   - Otherwise, in PLANNING, the first matching rule wins:
     - approvedPlanRevision !== planRevision gives replan ['approval-not-current'];
     - no valid planningEntry gives reassess ['planning-entry-unknown'];
     - entry.from AWAITING_APPROVAL, WORKING or REVIEW gives replan ['replan-requested-from-<FROM>'];
     - no basis gives reassess ['source-basis-missing'];
     - basis.planRevision !== planRevision gives reassess ['source-basis-stale'];
     - anything else gives pending [].
2. planSourcePaths(task). Pure.
   - affected is the sorted, unique union of the steps' affectedFiles. created is the same for newFiles, minus any path already in affected.
   - Each executionContract.sourceAssumptions[i] and executionContract.reuse[i] entry yields its own anchor list. Split the text on whitespace and the characters , ; : ( ) [ ] { } < > " ' ` #. Keep tokens that normalizeAffectedFile leaves unchanged and that contain '/' or end in a dot-extension.
   - More than 256 distinct paths in total sets tooMany.
3. assessPlanSource(projectRoot, { basisCommit, paths, candidate?: { baseRevision, deliveryTarget } }). Bounded, read-only Git through openProjectGit with a 5000 ms budget; export the seam `planReuseGit = { run: runGit }`.
   - Resolve HEAD with `rev-parse --verify --end-of-options HEAD^{commit}`. Check that the basis commit resolves to itself.
   - Run `ls-tree -r -z --full-tree --literal-pathspecs` for every referenced path at the basis. Run it at HEAD only when HEAD differs from the basis.
   - Keep mode, type and oid per path. A gitlink (160000) is recorded, not followed.
   - With a candidate, resolve `<deliveryTarget>^{commit}` after --end-of-options. A target that begins with '-' counts as unresolved.
   - It never throws. Any failure yields { unavailable: <first error line, at most 300 chars> }.
4. decidePlanReuse(paths, assessment). Pure. Returns { decision: 'reuse' | 'refresh' | 'reassess'; reasons; changedPaths; headCommit?; candidate? }.
   - Reassess reasons:
     - source-unavailable: <message>;
     - source-unavailable:gitlink:<path>;
     - too-many-source-paths;
     - assumption-unanchored:<sourceAssumptions|reuse>:<1-based index>, when no anchor of the entry exists at the basis;
     - assumption-changed:<path>, when an anchored path's mode or oid differs;
     - assumption-deleted:<path>;
     - affected-file-not-in-basis:<path>;
     - affected-file-deleted:<path>;
     - new-file-present:<path>, when a created path exists at HEAD.
   - Refresh reason: affected-file-changed:<path>. The path is also listed in changedPaths.
   - The candidate verdict is 'current' when the target resolves to candidate.baseRevision. Otherwise it is 'revalidate', with reason target-moved or target-unresolved. This never changes the decision on its own.
   - Precedence: any reassess reason gives reassess, else any refresh reason gives refresh, else reuse.
   - Reasons are sorted by code unit, deduped and capped at 32; when over the cap, keep 31 plus 'more-reasons:<n>'. changedPaths are sorted and capped at 64.

NOT in scope:
- state writes, task resumption, claim, wait or get_context integration (all CQ-C07);
- negative-search provenance (CQ-C05): until it lands, a path-less "no helper exists" reuse entry is unanchored and gets reassess;
- dirty worktree bytes (committed bytes only);
- symbol-level and check-definition comparison.

Verification command: cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test. Run it fresh; it must exit 0.

definitionOfDone:
planReuseView returns the exact decision and reasons for each rule, in table-driven vitest cases:
- no plan gives null;
- a non-PLANNING status without a record gives null;
- approval-not-current;
- planning-entry-unknown;
- replan-requested-from-AWAITING_APPROVAL, -WORKING and -REVIEW;
- BACKLOG and BLOCKED entries reach pending;
- source-basis-missing and source-basis-stale;
- a record matching planRevision and entrySeq answers;
- a record for an older entrySeq does not answer.

Against a real temporary Git repo, assessPlanSource plus decidePlanReuse give these results, each a named vitest case:
- an unrelated commit after the basis gives reuse, with empty changedPaths and headCommit != basisCommit;
- a changed affected file gives refresh, listing that file;
- a changed or deleted assumption path gives reassess with assumption-changed or assumption-deleted;
- a deleted affected file gives reassess with affected-file-deleted;
- an assumption with no anchor at the basis gives reassess with assumption-unanchored;
- a created file present at HEAD gives reassess with new-file-present.

Unavailable source yields reassess with a source-unavailable reason and never throws. Each is a named vitest case:
- a non-Git root;
- a basis commit that does not exist;
- a Git failure injected through planReuseGit.run;
- a gitlink path;
- more than 256 referenced paths gives too-many-source-paths.

Candidate verdicts, with the plan decision unchanged in every case (vitest cases):
- the delivery target branch still at candidate.baseRevision gives 'current';
- a target moved by a commit gives 'revalidate' plus target-moved;
- an unresolvable or '-'-prefixed target gives 'revalidate' plus target-unresolved.

implementationPlan.description:
Pure half of the new context/planReuse.ts (DoD 1). First read the LANDED CQ-C07a code: context/planReuseState.ts, and in types/schema.ts PlanSourceBasis, PlanningEntry, PlanReuseRecord and PlanReuseDecision. Use its exported names; if one differs from this plan, use the landed name and say so in the step note. Do not import state/taskStore.ts: this library stays pure.
(1) `export interface PlanSourcePaths { affected: string[]; created: string[]; anchors: { kind: 'sourceAssumptions' | 'reuse'; index: number; paths: string[] }[]; tooMany: boolean }`. index is 0-based; reasons print index + 1.
(2) planSourcePaths(task: Pick<Task,'implementationPlan'|'executionContract'>):
- affected: the sorted, unique union of the steps' affectedFiles.
- created: the same for newFiles, minus anything already in affected.
- Read every array defensively: a non-array or non-string entry contributes nothing.
- One anchor list per executionContract.sourceAssumptions[i] and reuse[i]. Every entry gets one, even an empty or non-string entry.
- Tokenize by splitting on /[\s,;:()[\]{}<>"'`#]+/. Trim trailing '.' and '/' from each token: this is a deliberate refinement, so a sentence-final 'util/x.ts.' still anchors.
- Keep a token only when normalizeAffectedFile(token) === token (catch its throw) AND (it includes '/' OR it matches /\.[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]{0,15}$/). Dedupe within each list.
- tooMany = the distinct union of affected, created and every anchor path has more than 256 entries.
- Every sort uses the default code-unit sort.
(3) planReuseView(task: Task): { decision: PlanReuseDecision | 'pending'; reasons: string[] } | null. Pure, and it never throws.
- revision: an absent planRevision reads 0; a non-negative safe integer reads as itself; anything else is null. This is decodeStoredPlanRevision's domain, but returning null instead of throwing.
- No implementationPlan steps returns null.
- record = readPlanReuseRecord(task) and entry = readPlanningEntry(task).
- The record answers with { decision, reasons: [...record.reasons] } when revision !== null && record.planRevision === revision && (status !== 'PLANNING' || (entry && record.entrySeq === entry.seq)).
- Otherwise, a status other than PLANNING returns null.
- In PLANNING, the first matching rule wins:
  - approvedPlanRevision is not a safe integer equal to revision: replan ['approval-not-current'];
  - no entry: reassess ['planning-entry-unknown'];
  - entry.from is AWAITING_APPROVAL, WORKING or REVIEW: replan [`replan-requested-from-${from}`];
  - readPlanSourceBasis(task) is null: reassess ['source-basis-missing'];
  - basis.planRevision !== revision: reassess ['source-basis-stale'];
  - otherwise: pending [].
(4) New context/planReuse.test.ts, table-driven. Use one valid PLANNING fixture: one plan step, planRevision 3, approvedPlanRevision 3, planningEntry { from: 'BACKLOG', at: <canonical ISO>, seq: 2 } and planSourceBasis { version: 1, commit: 'a'.repeat(40), planRevision: 3 }. Each row overrides one thing:
- no steps gives null;
- WORKING with no record gives null;
- approvedPlanRevision 2 gives approval-not-current;
- no entry gives planning-entry-unknown;
- from AWAITING_APPROVAL, WORKING or REVIEW gives replan-requested-from-X (3 rows);
- from BACKLOG or BLOCKED gives pending;
- no basis gives source-basis-missing;
- basis.planRevision 2 gives source-basis-stale;
- a record { planRevision 3, entrySeq 2, decision 'refresh', reasons ['affected-file-changed:a.ts'] } answers, in PLANNING and in WORKING;
- the same record with entrySeq 1 does not answer in PLANNING (the row is pending);
- a record for planRevision 2 does not answer.
planSourcePaths cases:
- union, sort and dedupe;
- created minus affected;
- the prose 'Uses `util/cachedPlanPaths.ts:106` (openProjectGit).' anchors ['util/cachedPlanPaths.ts'];
- a path-less entry gives an empty list;
- 257 distinct paths set tooMany.

Git half and decision (DoD 2, 3, 4). Error handling contract: assessPlanSource and decidePlanReuse NEVER throw.
(1) `export const planReuseGit = { run: runGit }`, mirroring requiredCheckGit in delivery/requiredChecks.ts.
(2) Export PlanSourceAssessment { basisCommit; headCommit; basis: Map<string, { mode; type; oid }>; head: Map<…>; target?: { baseRevision: string; commit: string | null } }. Use Maps, never plain objects keyed by repo paths.
(3) assessPlanSource(projectRoot, { basisCommit, paths: PlanSourcePaths, candidate?: { baseRevision, deliveryTarget } }): Promise<PlanSourceAssessment | { unavailable: string }>. One try/catch wraps the whole body; any throw becomes { unavailable: <first message line, at most 300 chars> }.
- paths.tooMany: unavailable, without spawning Git.
- basisCommit is not 40 or 64 lowercase hex: unavailable.
- `const git = await openProjectGit(projectRoot, planReuseGit.run, 5000)`. Read the seam at call time.
- resolve(rev) is the trimmed output of `rev-parse --verify --end-of-options <rev>^{commit}`.
- headCommit = resolve('HEAD'). resolve(basisCommit) must equal basisCommit.
- List the distinct union at the basis, and at HEAD only when HEAD differs from the basis: `git('ls-tree', ['--literal-pathspecs','ls-tree','-z','--full-tree', commit, '--', ...union], { maxBuffer: 1024 * 1024 })`.
- This is deliberately WITHOUT -r. Verified on git 2.43: ls-tree descends only as far as each pathspec needs and prints one entry per existing pathspec. A directory anchor prints its 040000 tree entry, whose oid changes when anything beneath it does. Output therefore stays bounded by the at most 256 pathspecs, whereas -r would expand a directory anchor to every blob beneath it.
- An empty union skips ls-tree: with no pathspec, Git lists the whole tree.
- Parse each NUL-terminated record with /^(100644|100755|120000|040000|160000) (blob|tree|commit) ([0-9a-f]{40}|[0-9a-f]{64})\t([\s\S]+)$/. Each of these throws: an unterminated listing, a record that does not match, a path that is not one of the requested pathspecs, or a duplicate path.
- With a candidate: a deliveryTarget that is not a non-empty string, or that starts with '-', gets commit null without running Git. Otherwise use try { resolve(target) } catch { null }.
(4) decidePlanReuse(paths, assessment) returns { decision: 'reuse'|'refresh'|'reassess'; reasons; changedPaths; headCommit?; candidate? }.
- tooMany: reassess ['too-many-source-paths'].
- unavailable: reassess [`source-unavailable: ${message}`].
- Otherwise, collect reasons:
  - mode 160000 at the basis or HEAD: `source-unavailable:gitlink:<path>`;
  - an affected or created path that fails C07a's path rule (normalizeAffectedFile(p) === p, no control characters): `source-path-invalid:<path>`. This is a new reassess code. It keeps every refresh's changedPaths recordable;
  - per anchor list:
    - none of its paths in the basis map: `assumption-unanchored:<kind>:<index+1>`;
    - otherwise, for each path present at the basis: missing at HEAD gives assumption-deleted:<path>, and a different mode or oid gives assumption-changed:<path>;
  - per valid affected path: absent at the basis gives affected-file-not-in-basis, absent at HEAD gives affected-file-deleted, and a different mode or oid gives affected-file-changed:<path> plus an entry in changedPaths;
  - each created path present at HEAD: new-file-present:<path>;
  - target: target.commit === baseRevision gives candidate 'current'. Otherwise the candidate is 'revalidate', with 'target-moved' (resolved) or 'target-unresolved' (null).
- Decision: any reason other than affected-file-changed:*, target-moved or target-unresolved gives reassess; otherwise any affected-file-changed gives refresh; otherwise reuse. The candidate verdict never changes the decision.
- Hygiene, because C07 persists this through C07a's validatePlanReuseRecord:
  - after composing each reason, replace control characters with '?' and clip it to 300 chars;
  - dedupe, code-unit sort and cap reasons at 32 (over the cap, keep the first 31 plus `more-reasons:<dropped count>`);
  - sort changedPaths and cap them at 64;
  - include headCommit whenever the source was available.
(5) Tests in context/planReuse.test.ts. Build a temp repo with fs.mkdtempSync under os.tmpdir() and the git() helper pattern from delivery/requiredChecks.snapshot.test.ts: GIT_* stripped, NOSYSTEM/GLOBAL masked, author env, core.autocrlf=false and empty core.hooksPath. Remove the repo in afterEach. Named cases:
- an unrelated commit gives reuse, changedPaths [], and headCommit !== basisCommit;
- a changed affected file gives refresh listing it;
- a changed assumption file gives assumption-changed, and a deleted one assumption-deleted;
- a deleted affected file gives affected-file-deleted;
- an unanchored assumption gives assumption-unanchored:sourceAssumptions:1;
- a newFile committed at HEAD gives new-file-present;
- a non-Git root, a nonexistent basis ('f'.repeat(40)), and vi.spyOn(planReuseGit,'run').mockRejectedValue(new Error('injected')) each give reassess with source-unavailable;
- a gitlink (git update-index --add --cacheinfo 160000,<hex>,vendor/sub, then commit) gives source-unavailable:gitlink:vendor/sub;
- 257 paths give too-many-source-paths, and the run spy is never called;
- candidates (decision stays reuse): refs/heads/target at the basis gives current; target moved with git commit-tree plus update-ref (HEAD unchanged) gives revalidate with target-moved; refs/heads/nope and '-x' give revalidate with target-unresolved.
Pure decidePlanReuse cases on synthetic Maps:
- 40 reasons collapse to 31 plus more-reasons:9;
- a 400-char reason is clipped to 300;
- a './a.ts' affected path gives source-path-invalid.
Guard: wrap every case's result as a PlanReuseRecord and assert validatePlanReuseRecord accepts it.
